ALGORITHM PARAM_SITE(request)

1. ROUTE
   IF request.path == "/"
      redirect to "/param/index.html"
   ELSE IF request.path == "/param/index.html"
      serve the public HTML page
   END IF

2. START PAGE
   Parse the HTML, load styles.css, then run main.js after parsing.

   Set motionEnabled to false if:
      reduced motion is requested, OR
      the connection requests data saving, OR
      the connection is 2G/slow-2G.
   Otherwise set motionEnabled to true.

   Update motion controls and register navigation, course, dialog,
   story, gallery, enquiry, reveal, tilt, and page-lifecycle handlers.

   Schedule the learning scene to load when the browser is idle,
   with a 1.8-second timeout; use a 500 ms timer if idle callbacks
   are unavailable.

3. PROCESS UI EVENTS
   ON navigation toggle:
      open or close the mobile menu
      close it after a link click, Escape, outside click, or desktop resize
      update the active section as the page scrolls

   ON course filter:
      show cards matching the selected category, or all cards
      update the selected filter and visible-course count

   ON course link:
      if the course has a detail page, select it and open its dialog
      show only that course's content
      otherwise follow the link to the enquiry section

   ON course-dialog enquiry:
      close the dialog
      reset the enquiry view
      preselect the chosen course and focus the name field

   ON story controls:
      move to the previous, next, or selected story
      wrap from the last story to the first, and vice versa

   ON gallery item or controls:
      open the image dialog with its image, alt text, caption, and count
      move between images with buttons or arrow keys, wrapping at either end

   ON generic dialog open/close:
      remember and restore focus
      pause the scene while a dialog is open
      resume it when all dialogs are closed and motion is enabled

4. PROCESS ENQUIRY SUBMISSION
   Prevent the browser's normal form submission.

   Clean the name and phone fields:
      replace control characters with spaces, trim, and limit their lengths
   Clean the optional note the same way, with a 500-character limit.

   Validate:
      name has at least 2 characters and contains a Unicode letter
      phone contains only an optional leading "+", digits, spaces,
         parentheses, or hyphens, and has 10–15 digits
      class is one of the form's listed options
      course is one of the configured course choices

   IF any validation fails:
      display every applicable error
      focus the first invalid field
      stop

   Build the enquiry message from the student's name, phone, class,
   course, and optional note.

   Create:
      a WhatsApp link with the message prefilled
      an email link to sb@goparam.com with a course-specific subject

   Show the prepared-message view and wait for the visitor to choose
   WhatsApp, email, or copy.
   The visitor must complete sending in their chosen app; the site
   does not submit the form to a backend or book a demo.

5. PROCESS MOTION AND PAGE LIFECYCLE
   Load the bundled scene only when motion is enabled and the scene
   is neither loaded, loading, nor marked failed.
   If scene loading or rendering fails, keep the static scene image
   and show the fallback status.

   Pause the scene when it is off-screen, the tab is hidden, motion
   is disabled, or a dialog opens.
   Dispose it when the page is closed; pause and resume it around
   back-forward-cache navigation.
